                "word": "physogastry",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8890c7d4-9580-38ce-8ddd-de3b3cea758e",
                        "entry_id": "537b1351-38c8-3d97-9a10-935d73787cdb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An enlargement of the abdomen in certain insects, especially in termite queens."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6211ae11-e410-49e9-8068-a2e3d12ed3bc",
                                "sense_id": "8890c7d4-9580-38ce-8ddd-de3b3cea758e",
                                "text": "One of the most bizarre modifications of the beetle abdomen is known as physogastry. Physogastry is a condition in which the abdomen is enlarged. usually through increased growth of the connective membranes, expansion of the internal fat bodies, and subsequent secondary sclerotization of the abdominal sclerites."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a0b512b3-4534-415b-bff6-40abde2f2302",
                                "sense_id": "8890c7d4-9580-38ce-8ddd-de3b3cea758e",
                                "text": "The development of queen physogastry is considered to mark the end of the founding stage. It is often difficult to determine the time required for a queen to become physogastric in termite colonies."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1868f2aa-0768-4425-8e1f-d6ab83112a8f",
                                "sense_id": "8890c7d4-9580-38ce-8ddd-de3b3cea758e",
                                "text": "The most striking characteristic of many termitophiles is physogastry, or the excessive enlargement of the abdomen, which closely resembles that of the hosts and especially that of the old queens."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
